# Product Requirements Document (PRD)
## Home Automation Product Catalog - Frontend UI (Phase 1)

---

## 1. Project Overview

### 1.1 Purpose
Build a frontend-only product catalog and ordering system for a home automation company website using React. This phase focuses on UI/UX with mock JSON data. Backend API integration will follow in Phase 2.

### 1.2 Technical Scope
- **Frontend**: React (existing website)
- **Data Source**: Local JSON file (mock data)
- **State Management**: React Hooks (useState, useContext) or localStorage
- **Routing**: React Router
- **Styling**: Tailwind CSS (or your preferred CSS framework)

### 1.3 Two Ordering Flows
1. **Cart Flow**: Add to Cart → Cart Page → Checkout → Payment Gateway
2. **Direct Order Flow**: View Product Details → Product Details Page → Submit Order Form

---

## 2. Features & Pages

### 2.1 Product Catalog Page (`/products`)

**Description**: Main page displaying all home automation products

**UI Components**:
- Header with company logo and cart icon (with item count badge)
- Product grid layout (responsive: 1 col mobile, 2-3 cols tablet, 3-4 cols desktop)
- Each product card shows:
  - Product image
  - Product name
  - Category badge (e.g., "Smart Lighting", "Security")
  - Brief description (1-2 lines)
  - Price
  - **Two buttons**:
    - **"Add to Cart"** (primary button - blue)
    - **"View Details"** or **"View Product"** (secondary button - green)

**Interactions**:

#### When "Add to Cart" is clicked:
1. **Modal/Popup appears** with:
   - Product image
   - Product name and price
   - **Quantity selector** (dropdown or +/- buttons: 1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 10, etc.)
   - Subtotal calculation (price × quantity)
   - Two buttons in modal:
     - **"View Cart"** → Navigate to cart page
     - **"Continue Shopping"** → Close modal, stay on catalog
2. Product added to cart with selected quantity
3. Cart icon badge updates with new item count

#### When "View Details" is clicked:
- Navigate to Product Details Page (`/product/:id`)

---

### 2.2 Add to Cart Modal (Popup)

**Description**: Modal that appears when "Add to Cart" button is clicked

**UI Components**:
- Modal overlay (darkened background)
- Modal content card (centered):
  - Close button (X icon in top-right corner)
  - Product image (medium size)
  - Product name
  - Price per unit
  - **Quantity selector**:
    - Input field with +/- buttons OR
    - Dropdown menu (1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 10, 15, 20, etc.)
  - **Subtotal display**: Price × Quantity (updates in real-time)
  - Success message: "✓ Added to cart"
  - Two action buttons:
    - **"View Cart"** (primary - takes user to cart page)
    - **"Continue Shopping"** (secondary - closes modal)

**Behavior**:
- Modal closes when clicking outside, pressing ESC, or clicking buttons
- Quantity updates subtotal in real-time
- Cart state updates immediately

---

### 2.3 Product Details Page (`/product/:id`)

**Description**: Full product information page with direct order form (bypasses cart)

**UI Layout**: Single page with sections

**Section 1 - Product Information** (Top):
- Back button to catalog
- Product image gallery (main image + thumbnails if multiple images)
- Product name (large heading)
- Category badge
- Price (prominent display)
- Stock availability
- **Detailed description** (full paragraph)
- **Specifications** (list format):
  - Technical specs
  - Dimensions
  - Compatibility
  - Warranty info
  - Features list

**Section 2 - Direct Order Form** (Below product info):
- Section title: "Order This Product"
- **Quantity selector** (same as modal)
- **Customer Details Form**:
  - Full Name * (required)
  - Phone Number * (required)
  - Email Address (optional)
  - Delivery Address * (required, textarea)
  - City * (required)
  - Postal/Zip Code
  - Additional Notes (optional, textarea)
- **Order Summary Box** (sticky sidebar on desktop):
  - Product name
  - Quantity selected
  - Subtotal
  - "Submit Order" button (large, green)

**Post-Submit**:
- Show success message: "Your order request has been submitted! Our customer service will contact you shortly."
- Log order data to console
- Reset form
- Option to go back to products or submit another order

---

### 2.4 Shopping Cart Page (`/cart`)

**Description**: View and manage all cart items before checkout

**UI Components**:
- Back button to products page
- Page title: "Shopping Cart"
- Cart items table/list showing:
  - Product image (thumbnail)
  - Product name
  - Price per unit
  - **Quantity controls** (- and + buttons)
  - Subtotal (price × quantity)
  - Remove button (trash icon)
- **Cart totals** (right sidebar or bottom):
  - Subtotal
  - Tax/Fees (if applicable) - optional
  - **Grand Total** (large, bold)
- Two action buttons:
  - **"Continue Shopping"** (secondary - back to catalog)
  - **"Proceed to Checkout"** (primary, large, green)

**Empty Cart State**:
- Icon/illustration (empty cart)
- Message: "Your cart is empty"
- "Browse Products" button

**Interactions**:
- Click + → Increase quantity, update subtotal
- Click - → Decrease quantity (remove if becomes 0)
- Click trash icon → Remove item from cart
- Cart persists using localStorage
- Real-time total calculations

---

### 2.5 Checkout Page (`/checkout`)

**Description**: Final step - collect customer details and payment info for cart orders

**UI Layout**: Two-column layout (single column on mobile)

**Left Column - Customer Details Form**:
- Section title: "Shipping Information"
- Form fields with icons:
  - Full Name * (required)
  - Phone Number * (required)
  - Email Address (optional)
  - Delivery Address * (required, textarea)
  - City * (required)
  - Postal/Zip Code
  - Additional Notes (optional, textarea)
- All required fields marked with asterisk (*)
- Form validation on submit

**Right Column - Order Summary & Payment**:

*Order Summary Card*:
- "Order Summary" heading
- List of cart items:
  - Product name × quantity = subtotal
  - (Show 3-4 items, then "Show more" if many items)
- Subtotal
- Shipping (if applicable)
- **Total Amount** (large, bold)

*Payment Gateway Section* (UI only - no functionality yet):
- Section title: "Payment Method"
- **Payment options** (radio buttons or tabs):
  - Cash on Delivery (COD)
  - Credit/Debit Card (UI placeholder)
  - Mobile Payment (UI placeholder)
- If "Cash on Delivery" selected:
  - Info badge: "💰 Pay when you receive your order"
  - Text: "Our customer service will contact you to confirm delivery details"
- If "Card" selected (UI only):
  - Card number input (placeholder)
  - Expiry date and CVV (placeholders)
  - Note: "Payment integration coming soon"

**Place Order Button**:
- Large, prominent button: "Place Order"
- Shows loading state when clicked
- Disabled if form invalid

**Post-Submit**:
- Show success modal/message: "Order placed successfully! Order #[NUMBER]. Our customer service will contact you soon."
- Log complete order data to console
- Clear cart (localStorage)
- Reset form
- Auto-redirect to products page after 3-4 seconds OR provide "Continue Shopping" button

